      "writtenOn": "2017-11-21T02:42:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This does make the assumption that the final call to add() is before the first call to sortedItems(), yeah. Do you think it would be reasonable to just panic if it is detected that add() is called after sortedItems()?\n\nFor \"or be completely invalid if another goroutine starts running sort.Slice\", that\u0027s why atomic.StoreInt32(\u0026s.sorted, 1) only happens after sort.Slice\n\n\nAlthough on second thought now I\u0027m thinking it\u0027s probably worth it to always acquire the lock, in favor of simplicity/clarity.",
      "parentUuid": "b315eb3f_ca7ec1ea",
      "revId": "2f234133d75e37474ebfd0d108ee8d408696b948",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
